  "slug": "pangenome-graphs-bd3e",
  "summary": "Recent preprints apply pangenome graphs and fast mismatch-rate statistics to ancient DNA and pathogen phylogenies.",
  "synthesis": "The three preprints share a focus on inference from incomplete or reference-dependent data. TrailMix uses a pangenome reference graph to estimate mixture proportions and phylogenetic placement of hominin mtDNA sources in ancient samples. The fastpmr method addresses scale, a pairwise mismatch-rate approach to relatedness inference reported to run over 1000 times faster than READv2 across the global ancient DNA record. The pathogen study is methodologically adjacent: machine learning with beam search locates unsampled regions in partially sampled phylogenies from the observed tree alone, tested on simulated data. Only TrailMix is graph-based, so the shared thread is inference that is either reference-aware or computationally scaled, applied to ancient and pathogen datasets.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
